# -*- text -*-
##############################################################################
#
#  ECLOUD dictionary additions -- AAA_ARCHITECTURE.md §4.3 ("Gap") and §12 Q7.
#
#  1. ChilliSpot vendor 14559: attributes that FreeRADIUS 3.2.10
#     share/dictionary.chillispot does NOT define (it stops at 1-9, 100-102)
#     but that uspot and CoovaChilli use.
#
#     Source of the names/numbers (Phase 2 evidence, A4 cache):
#       - uspot upstream radcli dictionary
#         f00b4r0/uspot files/etc/radcli/dictionary.chillispot l.12-14
#         (cached: /Users/danny/.claude/jobs/6ede8b14/tmp/p2/a4_src/uspot_git/files/etc/radcli/dictionary.chillispot)
#           ChilliSpot-Max-Input-Gigawords   21 integer
#           ChilliSpot-Max-Output-Gigawords  22 integer
#           ChilliSpot-Max-Total-Gigawords   23 integer
#       - CoovaChilli doc/dictionary.coovachilli l.29-53 (same vendor id 14559,
#         "CoovaChilli-" prefix): Session-State 15, Max-*-Gigawords 21-23, VLAN-Id 24
#         (cached: /Users/danny/.claude/jobs/6ede8b14/tmp/p2/a4_src/coova/doc/dictionary.coovachilli)
#
#     Naming: FreeRADIUS 3.x has no attribute aliases and a second VENDOR with
#     the same number (CoovaChilli = 14559) would change the names used when
#     DECODING vendor 14559 attributes, so everything is defined once under the
#     existing "ChilliSpot" vendor. ECLOUD adapters therefore emit
#     "ChilliSpot-*" names for both uspot and CoovaChilli; on the wire the
#     result is identical to CoovaChilli's own "CoovaChilli-*" definitions.
#
#  2. TIP / OpenWiFi vendor 0x0000e608 (58888) request TLV (NETWORK_INTEGRATION.md §4,
#     PHASE2_VALIDATION.md DT-03 "dump vendor TLV 0000e608 bytes"):
#     REQUIRES DEVICE TEST, not defined. No attribute definitions have been
#     verified from an authoritative source; until a capture (DT-03) shows the
#     TLV layout, FreeRADIUS keeps decoding it as an unknown VSA
#     ("Vendor-Specific" / Attr-26.58888.x), which rlm_rest still forwards.
#
#  3. Internal attributes (numbers 3000-3999 are never put in a RADIUS packet;
#     see the comment in the stock raddb/dictionary). They carry server-side
#     facts into the JSON rlm_rest posts to ECLOUD (policy.d/ecloud,
#     docs/contracts/aaa-authorize.md).
#
##############################################################################

BEGIN-VENDOR	ChilliSpot

ATTRIBUTE	ChilliSpot-Session-State		15	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ChilliSpot-Max-Input-Gigawords		21	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ChilliSpot-Max-Output-Gigawords		22	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ChilliSpot-Max-Total-Gigawords		23	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ChilliSpot-VLAN-Id			24	integer

# CoovaChilli-Session-State values (doc/dictionary.coovachilli l.31-42)
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	Authorized		1
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	NotAuthorized		2
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	Started			3
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	Stopped			4
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	UserLogoutUrl		10
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	IdleTimeoutReached	11
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	TimeoutReached		12
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	LogoutTimeReached	13
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	InDataLimitReached	14
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	OutDataLimitReached	15
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	TotalDataLimitReached	16
VALUE	ChilliSpot-Session-State	LocationChanged		17

END-VENDOR	ChilliSpot

# TIP vendor 0x0000e608 (58888): REQUIRES DEVICE TEST, not defined (see header).

#
#  ECLOUD internal attributes (never on the wire)
#
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Packet-Src-IP-Address	3000	string
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Packet-Src-Port		3001	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Packet-Dst-Port		3002	integer
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Client-Shortname		3003	string
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Decision			3004	string
#  Set in post-auth so /internal/aaa/post-auth learns the outcome (the JSON
#  body is the request list; reply attributes are not serialised by rlm_rest).
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Auth-Result		3005	string
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Reply-Class		3006	string
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Reply-Message		3007	string
#  Cycle A (D-044): set ONLY by sites-available/ecloud-inner (EAP-TTLS inner
#  request) so /internal/aaa/authorize knows User-Name is an inner identity;
#  the outer server deletes them (policy.d/ecloud ecloud_request_context).
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-EAP-Inner		3008	string
ATTRIBUTE	ECLOUD-Outer-User-Name		3009	string
